  "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt's The Human Condition offers a phenomenological and historical reexamination of the vita activa—specifically labor, work, and action—grounded in human plurality, natality, and the fragile boundaries between the public and private realms, while diagnosing the modern peril of world alienation and the rise of society."
